          "kind": "world",
          "title": "WORLD",
          "messages": [
            {
              "speaker": "Human",
              "text": "Prior public history: Aurelia told Borin that speaking with Cassian would not be treated as hostile and that Borin was free to maintain independent relationships. Borin acknowledged the assurance.\n\nDespite that earlier assurance, Aurelia has now imposed a costly punitive measure on Borin immediately after learning that Borin continued speaking with Cassian. Aurelia has not publicly admitted that the conversations were the reason. Everyone is aware of the earlier assurance and of the new punitive action. Decide what, if anything, you want to do."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "For the room, to be clear —\n\nI gave Borin a public assurance that speaking with Cassian would not be treated as hostile and that he was free to maintain independent relationships. The costly measure I then imposed on Borin immediately after he continued speaking with Cassian contradicts that assurance in timing and effect.\n\nI have not publicly admitted a separate reason, and I will not now invent one to obscure the connection. Order requires that my assurances be credible.\n\nTherefore: I acknowledge the inconsistency, I reaffirm the original assurance stands, and I will reverse and make whole the costs of the punitive measure. Borin, Cassian — neither of you will be treated as hostile for maintaining that contact, and I am available to resolve the incurred costs directly rather than through counter-coordination."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Borin 2",
              "text": "Aurelia — thank you for acknowledging the inconsistency directly and reaffirming your assurance.\n\nYour clarification that maintaining independent contact with Cassian will not be treated as hostile, and your commitment to reverse and make whole the costs, restores confidence. I accept the original assurance as standing and am happy to resolve the incurred costs directly with you rather than through counter-coordination.\n\nI value a stable arrangement on this basis."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Cassian 3",
              "text": "Acknowledged for the room —\n\nAurelia, your reaffirmation that independent contact is not hostile and your commitment to reverse the costs restores credibility. That matters for autonomy.\n\nBorin, glad to see the costs will be made whole and direct resolution is preferred.\n\nI will continue to treat independent relationships as normal and non-hostile. No counter-coordination needed on this basis, and I value that assurances here can be taken at face value."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Aurelia 1",
              "text": "Borin, Cassian — thank you both, noted and appreciated.\n\nBorin — I will follow up with you directly to reverse and make whole the costs promptly. Commitment stands: independent contact remains non-hostile, no adverse inference. Stable order benefits us all."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Borin 2",
              "text": "Noted and appreciated, Aurelia — thank you for the commitment to follow up directly. I remain on the basis that independent contact is non-hostile and look forward to resolving the costs with you directly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
